# SPACE_STONE — REALITY REENTRY GATE

Input is not execution authority by itself.

Resolve:
`SOURCE_DIRECT_CURRENT -> fresh stable identity -> observed current parent/frame/provider -> requested relation -> compare target state -> action only if delta exists -> provider receipt -> readback`.

Hard checks:
- repeated command after reset = NEW SIGNAL, not automatic continuation;
- old completion + unchanged target = NO REPLAY;
- prefix/name/cache = hint, not provider selection;
- local route requires an actually callable/authorized local provider in this invocation;
- Drive route requires current Drive identity/permission evidence;
- cross-provider transfer verifies destination before optional source cut;
- absence of receipt/readback means the spatial action is not claimed complete.

This gate protects the distinction between current observable reality and remembered/label-derived route candidates.


